From 8e2fbcc244139ab4c0edcdf3ee92cec93310a327 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:34:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/38] B70-C1-R1: C1 target-graph capture snapshots in host
 RAM; footprint in the memory profile

TargetGraphs.run snapshots every spec state row of the batch twice (initial,
expected_state) before capturing, plus a transient gather copy. On the device
that is ~0.45 GiB per request per rank per snapshot at TP2 (GDN state 2x of
TP4), allocated after the KV cache and never seen by the memory profiler:
TP2 warm-up (3 requests) OOMed at b70_target_graph.py:74 asking 1.27 GiB with
0.95 GiB free (measured at TP2). Reserving the snapshots
as they were would take ~3.6 GiB/rank at TP2 (4 slots), and at TP4 more than
the profiled activation headroom.

The snapshots now live in host RAM and move through the device in chunks of
<= 256 MiB (save, restore and the exact state compare); the bytes are copied
exactly, so the capture equality gate is unchanged. The remaining device
footprint (one chunk each way, 0.5 GiB) is checked inside the memory profile
after profile_run: if the profiled transient peak does not cover it, it is
allocated once there, so the profiled peak is max(activations, capture) and
KV sizing accounts for it (log line "B70-C1-R1"). When the transient already
covers it (TP4: 1.5 GiB) nothing is allocated: an unconditional 0.5 GiB
allocate/free moved non-torch memory by ~85 MB on two TP4 ranks (KV 344,706
-> 338,475 tokens in the first TP4 gate). Qwen4Exp + DFlash2 on XPU with
VLLM_XPU_C1_TARGET_GRAPH=1 only; elsewhere nothing changes.

CPU: tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_b70_target_graph_snapshot.py (9 passed).
